        }
      ],
      "links": [],
      "text": "NHSpeedy\n — \n8/2/26, 9:57 PM\nSunday, August 2, 2026 at 9:57 PM\nFirst, it seems like in order to get the boost from the cheep-cheep, you have to take a wider line. I am wondering if the wider line + no nisc is better than the tighter line + nisc. Secondly, I'm wondering about whether it is something you can get on a consistent basis, especially going for it on both laps which I assume you would be. I noticed the cheep-cheep doesn't bounce up and down on the same spot, it moves around a bit. Not sure if that has any impact on anything as far as consistency, but it's something I noticed. I tried it a little bit just now but I wasn't able to get the boost. The other thing that I am also wondering is that, based on what nekozuki said, it seemed like he was saying that there is a cycle and his pace was too fast to be able to get the boost. So based on that information it seems like there might be a limit as to how fast that strat can be, and maybe it is more worthwhile to not go for it"
    },
